   "The average score of a worker is a raw score of 43, which corresponds to the 49th percentile.",
   "Scores above the 50th percentile are indicative of clinically significant burnout, this suggests that the typical worker is at risk of burnout.",
   "If administered more than once a line graph will be produced for the total and subscale percentiles.",
   "Changes are evaluated against a miniminally important difference threshold of half a standard deviation or mor (Norman et al., 2003)."
